  },
  data: {
    LLM: "After the deal and discards, players in turn declare combinations (Tarots, Kings and Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois) and receive marques from opponents. Player to dealer's right leads; suit must be followed; if unable to follow, must play a trump (no need to overtake). Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Fool may be played as excuse (s'excuser) in any trick except the last; it is shown and discarded to holder's tricks and cannot be captured. At end of play, card points in tricks (plus discards) are counted; players below average pay the winner(s).",
    Player: "After the deal and discards, players in turn declare combinations (Tarots, Kings and Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois) and receive marques from opponents. Player to dealer's right leads; suit must be followed; if unable to follow, must play a trump (no need to overtake). Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Fool may be played as excuse (s'excuser) in any trick except the last; it is shown and discarded to holder's tricks and cannot be captured. At end of play, card points in tricks (plus discards) are counted; players below average pay the winner(s).",
    objective: 'Score marques by declaring combinations, winning Tarots in tricks, avoiding capture of Tarots, making Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I), and having above-average card points in tricks; losers pay the winner(s).',
    gameplay: "After the deal and discards, players in turn declare combinations (Tarots, Kings and Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois) and receive marques from opponents. Player to dealer's right leads; suit must be followed; if unable to follow, must play a trump (no need to overtake). Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Fool may be played as excuse (s'excuser) in any trick except the last; it is shown and discarded to holder's tricks and cannot be captured. At end of play, card points in tricks (plus discards) are counted; players below average pay the winner(s).",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit; if unable, play a trump. No obligation to overtake when playing trump.',
      'Fool (Math) may be played as excuse except in the last trick; holder must excuse before last trick or pay two marques to each opponent.',
      'Tarots (Kings, Fool, Trump I, XXI): winning one in a trick pays one marque from each opponent; losing one to an opponent pays one marque to each.',
      'Ultimo: win last trick with King or Trump I (Bagat) for 6 marques from each opponent; if King or Trump I played to last trick but does not win, pay 6 marques to each opponent.',
      'Card points: Tarots 5 each, Queens 4, Cavaliers 3, Jacks 2; total pack 74. Below 25 points = loser, 25+ = winner.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Three players, each playing for themselves; no partnerships.',
      deck: '66-card pack: Italian-suited Tarot (78 cards) with the lowest three cards of each suit removed. 22 triomphes (21 trumps I–XXI plus the Fool); 4 suits with 4 court cards (King, Queen, Cavalier, Jack) and 7 numerals each.',
      equipment: 'Tarot pack, counters (marques).',
      dealing: "Dealer shuffles; player to dealer's left cuts (cut card shown; if it is a Tarot, dealer receives one marque from each opponent). Dealer deals 4 rounds of 5 cards to each player, then one more card to each other player and 4 to himself: non-dealers receive 21 cards each, dealer 24. The two non-dealers each discard one card and the dealer discards four; no trumps or Tarots may be discarded (penalty: two marques to each opponent). Discards count in the discarder's favour at end of play.",
    },
    turnFlow: "After the deal and discards, players in turn declare combinations (Tarots, Kings and Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois) and receive marques from opponents. Player to dealer's right leads; suit must be followed; if unable to follow, must play a trump (no need to overtake). Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Fool may be played as excuse (s'excuser) in any trick except the last; it is shown and discarded to holder's tricks and cannot be captured. At end of play, card points in tricks (plus discards) are counted; players below average pay the winner(s).",
