    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 21 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Score marques by declaring combinations, winning Tarots in tricks, avoiding capture of Tarots, making Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I), and having above-average card points in tricks; losers pay the winner(s).',
      "Turn-flow example: After the deal and discards, players in turn declare combinations (Tarots, Kings and Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois) and receive marques from opponents. Player to dealer's right leads; suit must be followed; if unable to follow, must play a trump (no need to overtake). Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit. Fool may be played as excuse (s'excuser) in any trick except the last; it is shown and discarded to holder's tricks and cannot be captured. At end of play, card points in tricks (plus discards) are counted; players below average pay the winner(s).",
      'Scoring example: Marques are won or paid for: declarations (Tarots, Kings+Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois), playing or capturing Tarots in tricks, Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I), and card points (Tarots 5, Queens 4, Cavaliers 3, Jacks 2; pack total 74). Below 25 points = loser pays winner(s); above 25 = winner collects. After the hand, the player(s) with above-average card points (25 or more) win; the player(s) with below average (24 or less) pay. Two losers each pay the single winner per 5-point band below 25; two winners each collect from the single loser per 5-point band above 25. Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I) pays 6 marques from each opponent..',
    ],
